cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "WALL Pattern: Workflow At-a-glance, Live & Legible — a process wall format and renderer"
abstract: >
  An open pattern, format and renderer for process walls that answer where work is
  stuck and what changed, in the spirit of an andon board: grey is normal, and colour
  appears only where a step needs attention. A wall is two JSON files, a config that
  declares the structure and a feed that reports only what is true now; the renderer,
  a single self-contained HTML file, keeps the previous snapshot and computes the
  deltas. Both files are specified as JSON Schema 2020-12. Version 0.2: a working
  renderer and a schema-validated contract, with fictional examples and one real wall
  run on a case-review cycle. No research claim is made.
